            "name": "query - Application Gateways Grid"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Why Directly Uploaded Certificates Require Decoding\r\nAzure Application Gateway stores directly uploaded certificates as raw Base64 (`publicCertData`) without exposing an `expirationDate` property in Azure Resource Manager (ARM).\r\n\r\nTo display their **exact expiration date, days remaining, and expiry status** above:\r\n1. Select your **Log Analytics Workspace** in the top parameter dropdown.\r\n2. Run the included PowerShell script or schedule it in Azure Automation / Logic App:\r\n```powershell\r\n.\\scripts\\Sync-AppGatewayCertificatesToLogAnalytics.ps1 -WorkspaceId '<Workspace-ID>' -WorkspaceKey '<Workspace-Key>'\r\n```\r\nThe script decodes the X.509 certificate binary, extracts the `NotAfter` date, and ingests it into `AppGatewayCertificates_CL`.",
