          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Enabling Real-Time Expiry Alerts for Azure Key Vault\r\nBecause Key Vault stores certificate private keys securely within the data plane, Azure Resource Graph inspects the vault metadata. To alert on individual certificate expirations inside Key Vault:\r\n\r\n1. **Diagnostic Settings**: Route Key Vault `AuditEvent` logs to an Azure Log Analytics Workspace.\r\n2. **Runbook / Azure Policy**: Assign Azure Policy *'Certificates should have the specified maximum validity period'* or assign an Event Grid trigger when certificates near expiry (`Microsoft.KeyVault.CertificateNearExpiry`).\r\n3. **Log Analytics Query**:\r\n```kusto\r\nAzureDiagnostics\r\n| where Category == \"AuditEvent\"\r\n| where OperationName in (\"CertificateNearExpiry\", \"CertificateExpired\")\r\n| project TimeGenerated, Resource, OperationName, ResultDescription, CallerIpAddress\r\n```",
